{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And now, Israel, what does YHWH your Elohim ask of you, but to fear YHWH your Elohim, to walk in all His ways, and to love Him, and to serve YHWH your Elohim with all your heart and with all your soul.</b> He says: even though you provoked Him many times at Horeb and in the wilderness, behold He forgives you everything, provided that you fear Him from now onward." "<b>And Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote</b> that this entire verse extends as far as 'for your good' (לטוב לך) — that is, He asks nothing of you that is for His own need and not for yours, in the manner of (Job 35:7): ״אם צדקת מה תתן לו״. Rather, it is all לטוב לך — for your good. And He stated the reason: ״כי לה׳ אלהיך השמים ושמי השמים הארץ וכל אשר בה״ — for to YHWH your Elohim belong the heavens and the heaven of heavens, the earth and all that is in it — and all of them give glory to His name; He has no need of you. Rather, ״באבותיך חשק ה׳ ויבחר בזרעם בכם״ — in your fathers did YHWH set His desire, and He chose their seed after them — namely you, for you are the choicest of their seed, not Ishmael or Esau. And the sense of כיום הזה is כי כן יהיה בכל זרעם — thus shall it be for all their seed — end quote." "<b>It is known</b> what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded from this verse: that a person is obligated to recite one hundred blessings every day. For it is stated: מה ה׳ אלהיך שואל מעמך — 'What does YHWH your Elohim ask of you' — do not read מה but rather מאה, that is, one hundred — 'one hundred does YHWH your Elohim ask of you.'" "<b>And there are</b> in this verse ninety-nine letters, and with the alef that you place in the word מ״ה they complete one hundred letters, and the word becomes מאה, in order to hint by way of asmakhta that a person is obligated to recite one hundred blessings every day. And likewise there is an asmakhta for this from the verse (Psalms 128:4): ״הנה כי כן יבורך גבר ירא ה׳״ — 'Behold, for thus shall the man be blessed who fears YHWH' — one who fears YHWH must bless a count of כ״י כ״ן. Furthermore, (II Samuel 23:1): ״נאם הגבר הוקם על״ — fulfill ע״ל blessings. And they said that David, peace be upon him, instituted one hundred blessings, and afterward they were forgotten, and the Men of the Great Assembly returned and instituted them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:19.807267130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}